  "details": "Using the provided vrc_AvatarV3HandsLayer controller and the default proxy animations, transitioning from any state back to idle causes your hands in-game to snap back, rather than transition smoothly. This affects both VR and Desktop.\n\nThis is a non-issue inside the Unity Editor, but is present in-game once the avatar has been uploaded.\n\nDuplicating the proxy animations results in the same issues and the only solution around the problem is to either make or use a different idle hand animation.",
